{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hxyxfnalb7ctz7c5caqgkpbcdjn7q5scja5vnlmqyy3gfpmn27ua","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Rejection / error enumeration\n\n## Part 1 — `c_src/src/load.c`\n\nNotes that apply to every `error_set()` row: the message is post-processed by `error_set` (load.c:85-135) — if `lex` is non-NULL and `lex->saved_text` is non-empty **and** `saved_text.length <= 20`, the final text becomes `\"<msg> near '<saved_text>'\"`; if `saved_text` is empty, code `json_error_invalid_syntax` is silently **rewritten to `json_error_premature_end_of_input`** and text becomes `\"<msg> near end of file\"` (unless `stream.state == STREAM_STATE_ERROR`, in which case the raw msg is used with no context suffix). `error_set` with `!error` is a silent no-op.\n\n| function | trigger (exact condition / malformed input) | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `error_set` (load.c:95) | `if (!error) return;` — caller passed NULL `json_error_t*` | returns void, nothing recorded; caller still takes its failure path |\n| `error_set` (load.c:118-121) | `saved_text` empty && `code == json_error_invalid_syntax` | code silently upgraded to `json_error_premature_end_of_input` |\n| `stream_get` (load.c:154) | `stream->state != STREAM_STATE_OK` (sticky EOF/ERROR) | returns `STREAM_STATE_EOF` (-1) or `STREAM_STATE_ERROR` (-2) without reading |\n| `stream_get` (load.c:159-162) | `c == EOF` from `get()` | sets `state = STREAM_STATE_EOF`, returns `-1` (no error text) |\n| `stream_get` (load.c:171-173, out:) | lead byte `0x80..0xFF` with `utf8_check_first(c) == 0`: continuation byte `0x80..0xBF`, overlong lead `0xC0`/`0xC1`, or `>= 0xF5` | `state = STREAM_STATE_ERROR`, returns `-2`; `json_error_invalid_utf8`, text `\"unable to decode byte 0x%x\"` (no \" near \" context) |\n| `stream_get` (load.c:180, out:) | `!utf8_check_full(buffer, count, NULL)` — bad continuation bytes, overlong encoding, surrogate range, or `> U+10FFFF` | same as above: `-2`, `json_error_invalid_utf8`, `\"unable to decode byte 0x%x\"` |\n| `stream_get` (load.c:175) | `assert(count >= 2)` after non-zero `utf8_check_first` on a >=0x80 byte | abort in debug builds |\n| `stream_unget` (load.c:221) | `assert(stream->buffer_pos > 0)` | abort if ungetting with empty buffer |\n| `stream_unget` (load.c:223) | `assert(stream->buffer[stream->buffer_pos] == c)` | abort if ungot char != buffered char |\n| `lex_unget_unsave` (load.c:255) | `assert(c == d)` where `d = strbuffer_pop(&lex->saved_text)` | abort if popped saved char mismatches |\n| `decode_unicode_escape` (load.c:278) | `assert(str[0] == 'u')` | abort |\n| `decode_unicode_escape` (load.c:290) | any of the 4 chars after `u` is not `[0-9a-fA-F]` | returns `-1` (caller converts to an error) |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:308) | `c == STREAM_STATE_ERROR` mid-string (invalid UTF-8 inside string) | `goto out`; `token = TOKEN_INVALID`, string freed; error already set by `stream_get` (`json_error_invalid_utf8`) |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:311-314) | `c == STREAM_STATE_EOF` before closing `\"` — e.g. `\"abc` | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_premature_end_of_input`, text `\"premature end of input near end of file\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:320-321) | raw `\\n` inside string literal (`0 <= c <= 0x1F` and `c == '\\n'`) | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"unexpected newline\"` (+ near-context) |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:322-324) | any other raw control char `0x00..0x1F` inside string (e.g. raw TAB, 0x01) | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"control character 0x%x\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:333-336) | `\\u` followed by fewer than 4 hex digits, e.g. `\"\\u12g4\"`, `\"\\u1\"` | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"invalid escape\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:343-345) | `\\` followed by a char not in `\" \\ / b f n r t u`, e.g. `\"\\x\"`, `\"\\ \"` | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"invalid escape\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:358-362) | `jsonp_malloc(saved_text.length + 1)` returns NULL | `goto out`; `TOKEN_INVALID` with **no error text set at all** (documented as \"not very nice\") |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:375-379) | second pass: `decode_unicode_escape(p) < 0` on first escape | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, `\"invalid Unicode escape '%.6s'\"` (prints the 6 chars `\\uXXXX`) |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:386-390) | second pass: `decode_unicode_escape` of the *second* surrogate escape `< 0` | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, `\"invalid Unicode escape '%.6s'\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:394-402) | high surrogate `0xD800..0xDBFF` followed by `\\u` whose value is **not** `0xDC00..0xDFFF` (e.g. `\"\\uD800\\u0041\"`) | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, `\"invalid Unicode '\\\\u%04X\\\\u%04X'\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:404-408) | high surrogate `0xD800..0xDBFF` not followed by `\\u` at all (e.g. `\"\\uD800\"`, `\"\\uD800x\"`) | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, `\"invalid Unicode '\\\\u%04X'\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:410-413) | lone **low** surrogate `0xDC00 <= value <= 0xDFFF` (e.g. `\"\\uDC00\"`) | `TOKEN_INVALID`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, `\"invalid Unicode '\\\\u%04X'\"` |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:416-417) | `utf8_encode(value, t, &length)` non-zero → `assert(0)` | abort (considered unreachable) |\n| `lex_scan_string` (load.c:441-442) | `default: assert(0)` in the short-escape switch | abort (considered unreachable) |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:481-486) | leading zero followed by a digit, e.g. `01`, `-012` | returns `-1`, `token = TOKEN_INVALID`, **no error text**; surfaces later as `\"invalid token\"` from `parse_value` |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:491-494) | first significant char is neither `0` nor `1-9`: bare `-`, `-x`, `-.5` | returns `-1`, `TOKEN_INVALID`, no error text → later `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:505-509) | integer path, `errno == ERANGE` and `intval < 0` (e.g. `-99999999999999999999`) | returns `-1`; `json_error_numeric_overflow`, text `\"too big negative integer\"` |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:510) | integer path, `errno == ERANGE`, `intval >= 0` (e.g. `99999999999999999999`) | returns `-1`; `json_error_numeric_overflow`, text `\"too big integer\"` |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:514) | `assert(end == saved_text + lex->saved_text.length)` — strtoint didn't consume the whole token | abort in debug builds |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:521-526) | `.` not followed by a digit, e.g. `1.`, `1.e5` | returns `-1`, `TOKEN_INVALID`, no error text → `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:534-542) | `e`/`E` (optionally `+`/`-`) not followed by a digit, e.g. `1e`, `1e+`, `1ex` | returns `-1`, `TOKEN_INVALID`, no error text → `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `lex_scan_number` (load.c:551-553) | `jsonp_strtod()` fails (real out of double range, e.g. `1e999`) | returns `-1`; `json_error_numeric_overflow`, text `\"real number overflow\"` |\n| `lex_scan` (load.c:581-584) | `c == STREAM_STATE_ERROR` at token start (invalid UTF-8 outside a string) | `token = TOKEN_INVALID`; error already `json_error_invalid_utf8` |\n| `lex_scan` (load.c:616-617) | alpha identifier that is not exactly `true`/`false`/`null`, e.g. `nul`, `True`, `NaN`, `foo` | `token = TOKEN_INVALID` (no message here) → `parse_value` emits `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `lex_scan` (load.c:620-624) | any other byte: `#`, `'`, `@`, `(`, `+`, `.`, `)`, valid-but-unexpected UTF-8 char | `lex_save_cached()` then `token = TOKEN_INVALID` → later `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `lex_init` (load.c:644-645) | `strbuffer_init(&lex->saved_text)` fails (OOM) | returns `-1`; callers (`json_loads`/`loadb`/`loadf`/`loadfd`/`load_callback`) return `NULL` **with no error text set** |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:663-665) | `json_object()` returns NULL (OOM) | returns `NULL`, no error text |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:676-678) | token after `{` (or after `,`) is not a string and not `}` — e.g. `{1:2}`, `{,}`, `{` EOF | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"string or '}' expected\"` (empty saved_text → upgraded to `json_error_premature_end_of_input` + `\" near end of file\"`) |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:681-683) | `lex_steal_string()` returns NULL (token not TOKEN_STRING / already stolen) | returns `NULL` immediately, **no error text and `object` is not decref'd** (leak) |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:684-688) | object key contains an embedded NUL, i.e. `memchr(key, '\\0', len)` — e.g. `{\"a\\u0000b\": 1}` | `NULL`; `json_error_null_byte_in_key`, text `\"NUL byte in object key not supported\"` |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:691-696) | `flags & JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES` and `json_object_getn(object, key, len)` non-NULL — e.g. `{\"a\":1,\"a\":2}` | `NULL`; `json_error_duplicate_key`, text `\"duplicate object key\"` |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:700-703) | token after key is not `:` — e.g. `{\"a\" 1}`, `{\"a\",1}` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"':' expected\"` |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:707-711) | recursive `parse_value` returned NULL | `NULL`, error already set by callee |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:713-716) | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck()` non-zero (OOM / bad args) | `NULL`, **no error text set** |\n| `parse_object` (load.c:727-730) | after last member the token is not `}` — e.g. `{\"a\":1`, `{\"a\":1]` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"'}' expected\"` (or `premature_end_of_input` if at EOF) |\n| `parse_array` (load.c:740-742) | `json_array()` returns NULL (OOM) | `NULL`, no error text |\n| `parse_array` (load.c:749-751) | element `parse_value` returned NULL | `NULL`, error from callee |\n| `parse_array` (load.c:753-755) | `json_array_append_new()` non-zero (OOM) | `NULL`, **no error text set** |\n| `parse_array` (load.c:764-767) | after last element the token is not `]` — e.g. `[1,2`, `[1 2]`, `[1,]` (`,` then `]` → parse_value \"unexpected token\"), `while (lex->token)` exit on `TOKEN_EOF == 0` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"']' expected\"` (upgraded to `premature_end_of_input` at EOF) |\n| `parse_value` (load.c:779-783) | `++lex->depth > JSON_PARSER_MAX_DEPTH` (2048) — e.g. 2049 nested `[` | `NULL`; `json_error_stack_overflow`, text `\"maximum parsing depth reached\"`. (Depth is **not** decremented on any error path.) |\n| `parse_value` (load.c:790-795) | string value contains NUL and `!(flags & JSON_ALLOW_NUL)` — e.g. `[\"a\\u0000b\"]` | `NULL`; `json_error_null_character`, text `\"\\u0000 is not allowed without JSON_ALLOW_NUL\"` |\n| `parse_value` (load.c:834-836) | `case TOKEN_INVALID` — reached for bad identifier, bad number, unexpected byte, failed string malloc | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `parse_value` (load.c:838-840) | `default:` — token is `}`, `]`, `,`, `:` or `TOKEN_EOF`; e.g. `[,1]`, `[:]`, `}` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"unexpected token\"` (at EOF → `premature_end_of_input` + `\" near end of file\"`) |\n| `parse_value` (load.c:843-844) | constructor returned NULL: `jsonp_stringn_nocheck_own`, `json_integer`, `json_real`, `parse_object`, `parse_array` (OOM) | `NULL`, no additional error text |\n| `parse_json` (load.c:856-860) | `!(flags & JSON_DECODE_ANY)` and first token is neither `[` nor `{` — e.g. `\"foo\"`, `42`, `true`, empty input | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_syntax`, text `\"'[' or '{' expected\"`; empty input → `json_error_premature_end_of_input`, `\"'[' or '{' expected near end of file\"` |\n| `parse_json` (load.c:863-865) | `parse_value` returned NULL | `NULL` |\n| `parse_json` (load.c:867-874) | `!(flags & JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK)` and trailing token != `TOKEN_EOF` — e.g. `[1] garbage`, `{} {}` | `NULL`, result decref'd; `json_error_end_of_input_expected`, text `\"end of file expected\"` |\n| `json_loads` (load.c:909-912) | `string == NULL` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, text `\"wrong arguments\"`, source `\"<string>\"`, line/col `-1`, pos 0 |\n| `json_loads` (load.c:917-918) | `lex_init` failure | `NULL`, no error text |\n| `json_loadb` (load.c:950-953) | `buffer == NULL` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, `\"wrong arguments\"`, source `\"<buffer>\"` |\n| `json_loadb` (load.c:959-960) | `lex_init` failure | `NULL`, no error text |\n| `json_loadf` (load.c:980-983) | `input == NULL` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, `\"wrong arguments\"`, source `\"<stream>\"` (`\"<stdin>\"` if `input == stdin`) |\n| `json_loadf` (load.c:985-986) | `lex_init` failure | `NULL`, no error text |\n| `json_loadfd` (load.c:1017-1020) | `input < 0` (negative fd) | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, `\"wrong arguments\"`, source `\"<stream>\"`/`\"<stdin>\"` |\n| `json_loadfd` (load.c:1022-1023) | `lex_init` failure | `NULL`, no error text |\n| `fd_get_func` (load.c:997-1000) | `read()` returns != 1 (EOF or error), or `HAVE_UNISTD_H` undefined | returns `EOF` — read errors are indistinguishable from EOF |\n| `json_load_file` (load.c:1037-1040) | `path == NULL` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, `\"wrong arguments\"` |\n| `json_load_file` (load.c:1042-1047) | `fopen(path, \"rb\")` returns NULL | `NULL`; `json_error_cannot_open_file`, text `\"unable to open %s: %s\"` (path, `strerror(errno)`) |\n| `json_load_callback` (load.c:1094-1097) | `callback == NULL` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, `\"wrong arguments\"`, source `\"<callback>\"` |\n| `json_load_callback` (load.c:1099-1100) | `lex_init` failure | `NULL`, no error text |\n| `callback_get` (load.c:1072-1073) | `stream->len == 0 || stream->len == (size_t)-1` (callback signalled end or error) | returns `EOF`; callback error is indistinguishable from EOF |\n| `string_get` (load.c:893-895) | `c == '\\0'` in the input string | returns `EOF` — embedded NUL silently truncates input |\n| `buffer_get` (load.c:935-936) | `stream->pos >= stream->len` | returns `EOF` |\n\n## Part 2 — `c_src/src/pack_unpack.c`\n\n`set_error` records line/column/pos from `s->token` and a source tag (`\"<format>\"`, `\"<args>\"`, `\"<validation>\"`, `\"<internal>\"`).\n\n| function | trigger | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:134-141) | simple case, `va_arg` string is NULL and `!optional` (`s`, or `s` object key) | `NULL`, `has_error = 1`; `json_error_null_value`, text `\"NULL <purpose>\"` → `\"NULL string\"` or `\"NULL object key\"`, source `\"<args>\"` |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:136-140) | same but `optional` (format `s?` / `s*`) and arg NULL | `NULL`, **no error**; `pack_string` then yields `json_null()` for `s?` or `NULL` for `s*` |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:145-149) | `!utf8_check_string(str, strlen(str))` — invalid UTF-8 in the `s` argument | `NULL`, `has_error = 1`; `json_error_invalid_utf8`, `\"Invalid UTF-8 <purpose>\"`, source `\"<args>\"` |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:153-158) | `optional` (`s?`/`s*`) combined with `#`, `%`, or `+` — e.g. `\"s?#\"`, `\"s*+\"` | `NULL`, `has_error = 1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Cannot use '%c' on optional strings\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:161-164) | `strbuffer_init(&strbuff)` fails | `has_error = 1`; `json_error_out_of_memory`, `\"Out of memory\"`, source `\"<internal>\"` (note: execution continues into the loop) |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:167-171) | NULL string arg inside the `#`/`%`/`+` loop (e.g. `\"s+\"` with a NULL piece) | `has_error = 1`; `json_error_null_value`, `\"NULL <purpose>\"`, source `\"<args>\"`; eventually `NULL` |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:184-187) | `strbuffer_append_bytes` returns -1 (OOM) | `has_error = 1`; `json_error_out_of_memory`, `\"Out of memory\"`, source `\"<internal>\"`; returns `NULL` |\n| `read_string` (pack_unpack.c:201-206) | concatenated/length-limited result fails `utf8_check_string` (e.g. `\"s#\"` length cutting a UTF-8 sequence) | `NULL`, `has_error = 1`; `json_error_invalid_utf8`, `\"Invalid UTF-8 <purpose>\"`, source `\"<args>\"` |\n| `pack_object` (pack_unpack.c:224-228) | format string ends before `}` — e.g. `\"{\"`, `\"{s:i\"` | `NULL` (object decref'd); `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Unexpected end of format string\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `pack_object` (pack_unpack.c:230-234) | key position token is not `s` — e.g. `\"{i:i}\"`, `\"{[]:i}\"` | `NULL`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Expected format 's', got '%c'\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `pack_object` (pack_unpack.c:244-252) | `pack()` for the value returned NULL and the value's next token is not `*` — e.g. `\"{s:o}\"` with NULL json | `has_error = 1`; `json_error_null_value`, `\"NULL object value\"`, source `\"<args>\"`; `json_vpack_ex` returns NULL |\n| `pack_object` (pack_unpack.c:261-265) | `json_object_setn_new_nocheck()` non-zero | `has_error = 1`; `json_error_out_of_memory`, `\"Unable to add key \\\"%s\\\"\"`, source `\"<internal>\"` |\n| `pack_object` (pack_unpack.c:213) | `json_object()` returns NULL — **not checked** | NULL object is used; `json_object_setn_new_nocheck(NULL,...)` path |\n| `pack_array` (pack_unpack.c:289-294) | format string ends before `]` — e.g. `\"[\"`, `\"[i\"` | `NULL` (array decref'd); `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Unexpected end of format string\"`, source `\"<format>\"`; comment: \"Format string errors are unrecoverable\" |\n| `pack_array` (pack_unpack.c:300-308) | element `pack()` returned NULL and next token is not `*` | `has_error = 1` with **no message of its own** (relies on the inner error); returns `NULL` |\n| `pack_array` (pack_unpack.c:313-317) | `json_array_append_new()` non-zero | `has_error = 1`; `json_error_out_of_memory`, `\"Unable to append to array\"`, source `\"<internal>\"` |\n| `pack_string` (pack_unpack.c:345-346) | `read_string` returned NULL | `json_null()` if the token was `?` and `!has_error`; otherwise `NULL` |\n| `pack_object_inter` (pack_unpack.c:383-385) | `va_arg(json_t*)` is NULL for `o`/`O` and the next token is neither `?` nor `*` | `NULL`, `has_error = 1`; `json_error_null_value`