\"` (type name), source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:495-500) | tokens present after `!` or `*` inside an object format — e.g. `\"{s:i!s:i}\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Expected '}' after '%c', got '%c'\"` (`'!'` if strict==1 else `'*'`), source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:502-506) | format ends before `}` — e.g. `\"{\"`, `\"{s:i\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Unexpected end of format string\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:514-518) | key position token not `s` — e.g. `\"{i:i}\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Expected format 's', got '%c'\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:520-524) | `va_arg` key pointer is NULL | `-1`; `json_error_null_value`, `\"NULL object key\"`, source `\"<args>\"` |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:539-543) | key absent from object and not marked optional (`s?`) | `-1`; `json_error_item_not_found`, `\"Object item not found: %s\"`, source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:546-547) | recursive `unpack()` failed | `-1` (inner error kept) |\n| `unpack_object` (pack_unpack.c:584-590) | strict mode (`!` in format or `JSON_STRICT` flag) and object has keys never unpacked | `-1`; `json_error_end_of_input_expected`, `\"%li object item(s) left unpacked: %s\"` with comma-joined key list, or `\"<unknown>\"` if the strbuffer failed; source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:604-608) | `root && !json_is_array(root)` for format `[` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected array, got %s\"`, source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:614-619) | tokens after `!`/`*` inside array format — e.g. `\"[i!i]\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Expected ']' after '%c', got '%c'\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:621-625) | format ends before `]` — e.g. `\"[\"`, `\"[i\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Unexpected end of format string\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:633-637) | token not in `unpack_value_starters = \"{[siIbfFOon\"` — e.g. `\"[x]\"`, `\"[#]\"`, `\"[%]\"`, `\"[+]\"`, `\"[?]\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Unexpected format character '%c'\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:643-648) | `json_array_get(root, i)` NULL — more format items than array elements | `-1`; `json_error_index_out_of_range`, `\"Array index %lu out of range\"`, source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:651-652) | recursive `unpack()` failed | `-1` |\n| `unpack_array` (pack_unpack.c:661-665) | strict and `i != json_array_size(root)` (array longer than format) | `-1`; `json_error_end_of_input_expected`, `\"%li array item(s) left unpacked\"`, source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'s'` (pack_unpack.c:680-684) | `root && !json_is_string(root)` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected string, got %s\"`, source `\"<validation>\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'s'` (pack_unpack.c:690-694) | `const char **` target is NULL (and not `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY`) | `-1`; `json_error_null_value`, `\"NULL string argument\"`, source `\"<args>\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'s'` + `%` (pack_unpack.c:698-704) | `size_t *` length target is NULL for `\"s%\"` | `-1`; `json_error_null_value`, `\"NULL string length argument\"`, source `\"<args>\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'i'` (pack_unpack.c:717-721) | `root && !json_is_integer(root)` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected integer, got %s\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'I'` (pack_unpack.c:732-736) | `root && !json_is_integer(root)` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected integer, got %s\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'b'` (pack_unpack.c:747-751) | `root && !json_is_boolean(root)` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected true or false, got %s\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'f'` (pack_unpack.c:762-766) | `root && !json_is_real(root)` (an integer is rejected by `f`) | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected real, got %s\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'F'` (pack_unpack.c:777-781) | `root && !json_is_number(root)` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected real or integer, got %s\"` |\n| `unpack` case `'n'` (pack_unpack.c:807-811) | `root && !json_is_null(root)` | `-1`; `json_error_wrong_type`, `\"Expected null, got %s\"` |\n| `unpack` default (pack_unpack.c:814-817) | any other format char, e.g. `\"x\"`, `\"}\"`, `\"#\"`, `\"+\"` at value position | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Unexpected format character '%c'\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n| `unpack` cases `i`,`I`,`b`,`f`,`F`,`o`,`O` (724, 739, 754, 769, 784, 798) | target pointer is NULL — **no NULL check** (unlike `'s'`) | undefined behaviour / NULL dereference on assignment, not a rejection |\n| `json_vunpack_ex` (pack_unpack.c:883-887) | `root == NULL` | `-1`; `json_error_null_value`, `\"NULL root value\"`, source `\"<root>\"`, line/col `-1`, pos `0` |\n| `json_vunpack_ex` (pack_unpack.c:889-894) | `!fmt || !*fmt` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_argument`, `\"NULL or empty format string\"`, source `\"<format>\"`, line/col `-1` |\n| `json_vunpack_ex` (pack_unpack.c:901-904) | `unpack()` returned non-zero | `-1` (inner error preserved) |\n| `json_vunpack_ex` (pack_unpack.c:907-912) | trailing tokens after top-level value — e.g. `\"[i]x\"`, `\"ii\"` | `-1`; `json_error_invalid_format`, `\"Garbage after format string\"`, source `\"<format>\"` |\n\n## Part 3 — `c_src/src/hashtable_seed.c`\n\nNo `json_error_*` codes here; failures are signalled with `return 1` and silently fall back.\n\n| function | trigger | expected C result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `seed_from_urandom` (hashtable_seed.c:68-70) | `open(\"/dev/urandom\", O_RDONLY) == -1` | returns `1` (failure), `*seed` untouched |\n| `seed_from_urandom` (hashtable_seed.c:72, 85-86) | `read(urandom, data, 4) != 4` → `!ok` | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_urandom` (hashtable_seed.c:77-79) | fallback path: `fopen(\"/dev/urandom\",\"rb\")` returns NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_urandom` (hashtable_seed.c:81, 85-86) | fallback: `fread(data,1,4,urandom) != 4` | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:112-114) | `GetModuleHandle(\"advapi32.dll\") == NULL` | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:116-119) | `GetProcAddress(... \"CryptAcquireContextA\")` NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:121-123) | `GetProcAddress(... \"CryptGenRandom\")` NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:125-128) | `GetProcAddress(... \"CryptReleaseContext\")` NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:130-132) | `CryptAcquireContext(..., PROV_RSA_FULL, CRYPT_VERIFYCONTEXT)` fails | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:134, 137-138) | `CryptGenRandom` fails | returns `1` (context still released) |\n| `generate_seed` (:181-185) | all strong sources failed (`!done`) | silently falls back to `seed_from_timestamp_and_pid` (always returns 0) — weak, predictable seed, no error reported |\n| `generate_seed` (:188-189) | `seed == 0` after generation | forces `seed = 1` (zero is reserved as \"uninitialized\") |\n| `json_object_seed` (all 4 variants: :202, :223, :250, :270) | `hashtable_seed != 0` (already seeded) | silent no-op; caller-supplied seed is ignored |\n| `json_object_seed` (:205-206, :224-229, :253-254, :271-272) | caller passes `seed == 0` | treated as \"pick one for me\": `new_seed = generate_seed()` |\n| `json_object_seed` (:209-216 / :232-242 / :257-262) | lost the race to another thread | busy-waits (`sched_yield()` / `SwitchToThread()`) until `hashtable_seed != 0`; no failure path |\n| `json_object_seed` fallback (:265-276) | neither atomic nor sync builtins nor `_WIN32` available | thread-unsafe version compiled; concurrent seeding is a data race, no diagnostic |\n\n## Part 4 — `c_src/include/jansson_private.h`\n\nContains **no** rejection logic at all. Relevant items:\n\n| item | detail |\n|---|---|\n| `container_of(ptr_, type_, member_)` | `((type_ *)((char *)ptr_ - offsetof(type_, member_)))` — used