ok` | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_urandom` (hashtable_seed.c:77-79) | fallback path: `fopen(\"/dev/urandom\",\"rb\")` returns NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_urandom` (hashtable_seed.c:81, 85-86) | fallback: `fread(data,1,4,urandom) != 4` | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:112-114) | `GetModuleHandle(\"advapi32.dll\") == NULL` | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:116-119) | `GetProcAddress(... \"CryptAcquireContextA\")` NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:121-123) | `GetProcAddress(... \"CryptGenRandom\")` NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:125-128) | `GetProcAddress(... \"CryptReleaseContext\")` NULL | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:130-132) | `CryptAcquireContext(..., PROV_RSA_FULL, CRYPT_VERIFYCONTEXT)` fails | returns `1` |\n| `seed_from_windows_cryptoapi` (:134, 137-138) | `CryptGenRandom` fails | returns `1` (context still released) |\n| `generate_seed` (:181-185) | all strong sources failed (`!done`) | silently falls back to `seed_from_timestamp_and_pid` (always returns 0) — weak, predictable seed, no error reported |\n| `generate_seed` (:188-189) | `seed == 0` after generation | forces `seed = 1` (zero is reserved as \"uninitialized\") |\n| `json_object_seed` (all 4 variants: :202, :223, :250, :270) | `hashtable_seed != 0` (already seeded) | silent no-op; caller-supplied seed is ignored |\n| `json_object_seed` (:205-206, :224-229, :253-254, :271-272) | caller passes `seed == 0` | treated as \"pick one for me\": `new_seed = generate_seed()` |\n| `json_object_seed` (:209-216 / :232-242 / :257-262) | lost the race to another thread | busy-waits (`sched_yield()` / `SwitchToThread()`) until `hashtable_seed != 0`; no failure path |\n| `json_object_seed` fallback (:265-276) | neither atomic nor sync builtins nor `_WIN32` available | thread-unsafe version compiled; concurrent seeding is a data race, no diagnostic |\n\n## Part 4 — `c_src/include/jansson_private.h`\n\nContains **no** rejection logic at all. Relevant items:\n\n| item | detail |\n|---|---|\n| `container_of(ptr_, type_, member_)` | `((type_ *)((char *)ptr_ - offsetof(type_, member_)))` — used by `stream_to_lex` in load.c; no NULL check |\n| `max(a, b)` | `((a) > (b) ? (a) : (b))`, only defined `#ifndef max` |\n| `va_copy` fallback | `__va_copy` if available, else `memcpy(&(a), &(b), sizeof(va_list))` |\n| `LOOP_KEY_LEN` | `(2 + (sizeof(json_t *) * 2) + 1)` = **19** on 64-bit, 11 on 32-bit |\n| `JANSSON_ATTRS((warn_unused_result))` | on `jsonp_malloc`, `jsonp_realloc`, `jsonp_strndup` — compile-time enforcement that allocation failures be checked |\n| `snprintf`/`vsnprintf` remap | `_snprintf`/`_vsnprintf` on MSVC `< 1900` / `< 1500` — these do **not** NUL-terminate on truncation, which is why load.c manually writes `msg_text[JSON_ERROR_TEXT_LENGTH - 1] = '\\0'` |\n\n## Named constants and limits\n\n| constant | value | file | role |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `STREAM_STATE_OK` | `0` | load.c:28 | normal stream state |\n| `STREAM_STATE_EOF` | `-1` | load.c:29 | sticky EOF; also a sentinel returned from `stream_get` |\n| `STREAM_STATE_ERROR` | `-2` | load.c:30 | sticky UTF-8 decode error; suppresses the `\" near end of file\"` context suffix |\n| `TOKEN_INVALID` | `-1` | load.c:32 | → `\"invalid token\"` |\n| `TOKEN_EOF` | `0` | load.c:33 | falsy, so `while (lex->token)` in `parse_array` terminates on EOF |\n| `TOKEN_STRING` | `256` | load.c:34 | |\n| `TOKEN_INTEGER` | `257` | load.c:35 | |\n| `TOKEN_REAL` | `258` | load.c:36 | |\n| `TOKEN_TRUE` | `259` | load.c:37 | |\n| `TOKEN_FALSE` | `260` | load.c:38 | |\n| `TOKEN_NULL` | `261` | load.c:39 | |\n| single-char tokens | the literal byte value | load.c:588-589 | `{ } [ ] : ,` are their own token values |\n| `MAX_BUF_LEN` | `1024` | load.c:1055 | `json_load_callback` buffer size passed to the callback |\n| `stream_t::buffer` | `char[5]` | load.c:57 | holds at most a 4-byte UTF-8 sequence + NUL |\n| `JSON_PARSER_MAX_DEPTH` | `2048` | include/jansson_config.h:10 | `parse_value` rejects `depth > 2048` with `json_error_stack_overflow` |\n| `JSON_ERROR_TEXT_LENGTH` | `160` | include/jansson.h:149 | error text buffer; last byte stores the `json_error_code` |\n| `JSON_ERROR_SOURCE_LENGTH` | `80` | include/jansson.h:150 | |\n| saved-text context cutoff | `20` | load.c:111 | `\" near '%s'\"` only appended when `saved_text.length <= 20` |\n| control-char range | `0 <= c <= 0x1F` | load.c:317 | rejected raw inside strings |\n| surrogate ranges | high `0xD800..0xDBFF`, low `0xDC00..0xDFFF` | load.c:383, 394, 410 | pairing validation for `\\u` escapes |\n| BMP offset | `0x10000` | load.c:397 | surrogate-pair recombination |\n| UTF-8 lead-byte gates (utf.c) | `<0x80`→1, `0x80..0xBF`→0, `0xC0/0xC1`→0, `0xC2..0xDF`→2, `0xE0..0xEF`→3, `0xF0..0xF4`→4, `>=0xF5`→0 | utf.c:38-67 | zero ⇒ `\"unable to decode byte 0x%x\"` |\n| decoder flags | `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES 0x1`, `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK 0x2`, `JSON_DECODE_ANY 0x4`, `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL 0x8`, `JSON_ALLOW_NUL 0x10` | jansson.h:358-362 | each gates a rejection branch in load.c |\n| unpack flags | `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY 0x1`, `JSON_STRICT 0x2` | jansson.h:332-333 | `JSON_STRICT` promotes `strict` to 1 ⇒ leftover-item errors |\n| `unpack_value_starters` | `\"{[siIbfFOon\"` | pack_unpack.c:42 | whitelist enforced only inside `unpack_array` |\n| `type_names[]` | `{\"object\",\"array\",\"string\",\"integer\",\"real\",\"true\",\"false\",\"null\"}` | pack_unpack.c:37-38 | indexed by `json_typeof(x)`; supplies the `got %s` text |\n| `json_error_code` enum | `unknown 0, out_of_memory 1, stack_overflow 2, cannot_open_file 3, invalid_argument 4, invalid_utf8 5, premature_end_of_input 6, end_of_input_expected 7, invalid_syntax 8, invalid_format 9, wrong_type 10, null_character 11, null_value 12, null_byte_in_key 13, duplicate_key 14, numeric_overflow 15, item_not_found 16, index_out_of_range 17` | jansson.h:160-179 | |\n\nCodes actually produced by these three files: load.c uses `invalid_utf8`, `premature_end_of_input`, `invalid_syntax`, `numeric_overflow`, `null_byte_in_key`, `duplicate_key`, `null_character`, `stack_overflow`, `end_of_input_expected`, `invalid_argument`, `cannot_open_file`. pack_unpack.c uses `null_value`, `invalid_utf8`, `invalid_format`, `out_of_memory`, `numeric_overflow`, `wrong_type`, `item_not_found`, `index_out_of_range`, `end_of_input_expected`, `invalid_argument`. Never produced by these files: `json_error_unknown`, and `out_of_memory`/`stack_overflow` are absent from load.c (its OOM paths return NULL with **no** error code, leaving whatever `jsonp_error_init` set).\n\n## Valid pack/unpack format characters\n\n### `json_pack` family (`pack()`, pack_unpack.c:423-461)\n\n| char | consumes (varargs) | notes / modifiers |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{` … `}` | alternating key/value | keys must be `s`; unterminated ⇒ \"Unexpected end of format string\" |\n| `[` … `]` | values | unterminated ⇒ \"Unexpected end of format string\" |\n| `s` | `const char *` | modifiers: `?` (NULL ⇒ JSON null), `*` (NULL ⇒ omit item), `#` (`int` length), `%` (`size_t` length), `+` (concatenate next string). `?`/`*` cannot combine with `#`/`%`/`+`. UTF-8 validated. |\n| `n` | nothing | JSON null |\n| `b` | `int` | non-zero ⇒ true, zero ⇒ false; never fails |\n| `i` | `int` | via `pack_integer`; only OOM fails |\n| `I` | `json_int_t` | via `pack_integer` |\n| `f` | `double` | non-finite ⇒ \"Invalid floating point value\" (`numeric_overflow`) |\n| `O` | `json_t *` | increments refcount; NULL ⇒ \"NULL object\" unless `?`/`*` |\n| `o` | `json_t *` | steals reference; NULL ⇒ \"NULL object\" unless `?`/`*` |\n| `?` / `*` | — | suffix modifiers for `s`, `o`, `O` (and `*` on an object/array member makes a NULL value omit the item) |\n| `#` / `%` / `+` | `int` / `size_t` / — | length and concatenation modifiers for `s` only |\n| ` ` `\\t` `\\n` `,` `:` | — | ignored/whitespace in `next_token` (pack_unpack.c:76) |\n| anything else | — | \"Unexpected format character '%c'\" (`invalid_format`). Note `F`, `!` are **not** valid for pack. |\n\n### `json_unpack` family (`unpack()`, pack_unpack.c:671-819)\n\n| char | consumes (varargs) | required root type / notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `{` … `}` | key/value pairs | root must be an object; keys must be `s` with a `const char *` arg |\n| `[` … `]` | values | root must be an array; only chars in `\"{[siIbfFOon\"` allowed as element starters |\n| `s` | `const char **` | root must be a string; NULL target ⇒ \"NULL string argument\"; optional `%` takes `size_t *` (NULL ⇒ \"NULL string length argument\") |\n| `i` | `int *` | root must be integer (truncating cast); target not NULL-checked |\n| `I` | `json_int_t *` | root must be integer; target not NULL-checked |\n| `b` | `int *` | root must be boolean; receives `json_is_true(root)` |\n| `f` | `double *` | root must be **real** (an integer is rejected) |\n| `F` | `double *` | root may be real **or** integer (`json_is_number`) |\n| `O` | `json_t **` | any type; increments refcount (unless `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY`) |\n| `o` | `json_t **` | any type; borrowed reference |\n| `n` | nothing | root must be JSON null; validate-only, never assigns |\n| `?` | — | after a `{`-object key: marks that key optional (missing key is not an error) |\n| `!` | — | inside `{}`/`[]`: require all remaining items consumed; any token after it ⇒ \"Expected '}'/']' after '!', got '%c'\" |\n| `*` | — | inside `{}`/`[]`: explicitly non-strict; any token after it ⇒ \"Expected '}'/']' after '*', got '%c'\" |\n| `%` | `size_t *` | only valid immediately after `s` |\n| ` ` `\\t` `\\n` `,` `:` | — | ignored |\n| anything else | — | \"Unexpected format character '%c'\" (`invalid_format`, returns -1). Note `#` and `+` are pack-only and are rejected here. |","usage":{"total_tokens":54222,"tool_uses":6,"duration_ms":219108},"uuid":"754e6c94-9c32-4963-b0f1-f4292a799544","session_id":"db0c18e4-4025-4f1b-bc6c-7708c62dcd24"}
