{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_6k6hnaofudkgizrufztqe2zlvvvedmugbgcia5obdfd47mqzdzyq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_016D7RnsAriHvLhquKgerwnb","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-RK3msz/translation/CONFIGS.md","content":"# CONFIGS.md — configuration-surface table (valid inputs)\n\nDerived mechanically from the branches the C actually takes on runtime options\nand input shapes. Every row is a *combination* (options set × input shape) the C\ntreats differently. Each row is driven through BOTH `.so`s with **many\nrandomized inputs** (SplitMix64, fixed seed) and compared byte-for-byte.\n\nBuild config that pins several axes (`c_src/include/jansson_config.h`,\n`jansson_private_config.h`):\n`JSON_INTEGER_IS_LONG_LONG=1` (`json_int_t` = `long long`),\n`JSON_PARSER_MAX_DEPTH=2048`, `DTOA_ENABLED=1`, `INITIAL_HASHTABLE_ORDER=3`\n(8 buckets), `HAVE_UNISTD_H`, `USE_URANDOM=1`.\n`jansson_config.h` does **not** define `JSON_HAVE_ATOMIC_BUILTINS` /\n`JSON_HAVE_SYNC_BUILTINS`, so the header's `json_incref`/`json_decref` use\nplain `++`/`--`; the harness replicates that exactly.\n\n## Axes\n\n**Decode flags** (`load.c`): `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES 0x1`,\n`JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK 0x2`, `JSON_DECODE_ANY 0x4`,\n`JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL 0x8`, `JSON_ALLOW_NUL 0x10`.\n\n**Encode flags** (`dump.c`): indent = bits 0..4 (`JSON_MAX_INDENT 0x1F`),\n`JSON_COMPACT 0x20`, `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII 0x40`, `JSON_SORT_KEYS 0x80`,\n`JSON_PRESERVE_ORDER 0x100` (**referenced nowhere in any `.c` — a true\nno-op**), `JSON_ENCODE_ANY 0x200`, `JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH 0x400`,\nprecision = bits 11..15, `JSON_EMBED 0x10000` (root only — the bit is stripped\nbefore recursion).\n\n**Unpack flags** (`pack_unpack.c`): `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY 0x1` (consumes no value\nvarargs; object *keys* are still consumed), `JSON_STRICT 0x2` (implicit `!` on\nevery container; a local `*` overrides it).\n\n**Growth thresholds to straddle:** hashtable rehash when `size >= hashsize(order)`\n→ at the 9th, 17th, 33rd, 65th, 129th, … distinct key (an *overwrite* of the 8th\nkey also triggers it). Array capacity 8 → `max(size+amount, size*2)`.\nstrbuffer 16 → `max(size*2, length+size+1)`.\n\n---\n\n## A. Encoding — `json_dump_callback` (low level) and all five wrappers\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| A1 | `json_dumps` | flags 0; random nested object/array trees, depth 1..6, all 8 types | [ ] |\n| A2 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_COMPACT` only, indent 0 → `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}` separators | [ ] |\n| A3 | `json_dumps` | indent 0, no compact → `\": \"` and `\", \"` separators | [ ] |\n| A4 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_INDENT(n)` for **every** n in 1..31, plus 0 and 32 (32 masks to 0) | [ ] |\n| A5 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_INDENT(31)` × depth ≥ 2 — indentation exceeds the 32-byte `whitespace[]`, forcing multi-chunk emission | [ ] |\n| A6 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_INDENT(n) \\| JSON_COMPACT` — indent branch wins, but separator is still `\":\"` (the compact branch of `dump_indent` is dead) | [ ] |\n| A7 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` off, random valid UTF-8 (1/2/3/4-byte) — verbatim run copying | [ ] |\n| A8 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` on, BMP codepoints → `\\uXXXX` (6 chars) | [ ] |\n| A9 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` on, non-BMP ≥ 0x10000 → recomputed surrogate pair `\\uXXXX\\uXXXX` (12 chars) | [ ] |\n| A10 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` on, exactly 0x7F (DEL) — *not* escaped (`> 0x7F` is false) | [ ] |\n| A11 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH` off vs on, strings containing `/` | [ ] |\n| A12 | `json_dumps` | short escapes `\\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\\" \\\\` and `\\u00XX` for the other `< 0x20` control chars | [ ] |\n| A13 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_SORT_KEYS` on — `compare_keys` = `memcmp` over `min(len)` then `len1-len2`; keys sharing prefixes, differing leng