"a\"` colliding | [ ] |\n| B5 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_REJECT_DUPLICATES` on — first repeat aborts | [ ] |\n| B6 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` off — trailing garbage rejected | [ ] |\n| B7 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_DISABLE_EOF_CHECK` on — trailing bytes ignored; `error->position` is the offset after the value only | [ ] |\n| B8 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL` off — pure integers → `JSON_INTEGER` via `strtoll` | [ ] |\n| B9 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_DECODE_INT_AS_REAL` on — integers become `JSON_REAL`; `12345678901234567890` no longer errors, re-encodes as `X.0`; overflow now says `\"real number overflow\"` | [ ] |\n| B10 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` on — `\u0000` in a string *value* accepted; length-aware retrieval | [ ] |\n| B11 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` on — `\u0000` in an object *key* still rejected (unconditional) | [ ] |\n| B12 | `json_loadb` | `JSON_ALLOW_NUL` on — a *raw* 0x00 byte in a string is still a control-char error | [ ] |\n| B13 | `json_loadb` | integer boundaries: `9223372036854775807`, `-9223372036854775808`, `-0`, and one past each bound | [ ] |\n| B14 | `json_loadb` | number grammar accepts: `0`, `-0`, `1e5`, `1E5`, `1e+5`, `1e-5`, `0.5`, `-0.0`, `1.5e-300`; underflow `1e-400` → `0.0` **silently, no error** | [ ] |\n| B15 | `json_loadb` | `\\u` escapes: all 1/2/3-byte BMP results, valid surrogate pairs `😀` → U+1F600 | [ ] |\n| B16 | `json_loadb` | valid multi-byte UTF-8 (2/3/4-byte) in keys and values; `column` counts *characters*, `position` counts *bytes* | [ ] |\n| B17 | `json_loadb` | all 9 valid string escapes `\\\" \\\\ \\/ \\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\uXXXX` | [ ] |\n| B18 | `json_loadb` | nesting depth exactly 2048 (accepted) and 2049 (rejected); mixed `[`/`{` nesting | [ ] |\n| B19 | `json_loadb` | object sizes straddling every rehash threshold: 0,1,7,8,9,15,16,17,31,32,33,63,64,65,127,128,129,255,256,257 distinct keys | [ ] |\n| B20 | `json_loadb` | overwriting the 8th key (triggers a rehash even though `size` does 