e bit is stripped\nbefore recursion).\n\n**Unpack flags** (`pack_unpack.c`): `JSON_VALIDATE_ONLY 0x1` (consumes no value\nvarargs; object *keys* are still consumed), `JSON_STRICT 0x2` (implicit `!` on\nevery container; a local `*` overrides it).\n\n**Growth thresholds to straddle:** hashtable rehash when `size >= hashsize(order)`\n→ at the 9th, 17th, 33rd, 65th, 129th, … distinct key (an *overwrite* of the 8th\nkey also triggers it). Array capacity 8 → `max(size+amount, size*2)`.\nstrbuffer 16 → `max(size*2, length+size+1)`.\n\n---\n\n## A. Encoding — `json_dump_callback` (low level) and all five wrappers\n\n| # | entry point(s) | configuration (options set + input shape) | [ ] |\n|---|----------------|--------------------------------------------|-----|\n| A1 | `json_dumps` | flags 0; random nested object/array trees, depth 1..6, all 8 types | [ ] |\n| A2 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_COMPACT` only, indent 0 → `{\"a\":1,\"b\":2}` separators | [ ] |\n| A3 | `json_dumps` | indent 0, no compact → `\": \"` and `\", \"` separators | [ ] |\n| A4 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_INDENT(n)` for **every** n in 1..31, plus 0 and 32 (32 masks to 0) | [ ] |\n| A5 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_INDENT(31)` × depth ≥ 2 — indentation exceeds the 32-byte `whitespace[]`, forcing multi-chunk emission | [ ] |\n| A6 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_INDENT(n) \\| JSON_COMPACT` — indent branch wins, but separator is still `\":\"` (the compact branch of `dump_indent` is dead) | [ ] |\n| A7 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` off, random valid UTF-8 (1/2/3/4-byte) — verbatim run copying | [ ] |\n| A8 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` on, BMP codepoints → `\\uXXXX` (6 chars) | [ ] |\n| A9 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` on, non-BMP ≥ 0x10000 → recomputed surrogate pair `\\uXXXX\\uXXXX` (12 chars) | [ ] |\n| A10 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENSURE_ASCII` on, exactly 0x7F (DEL) — *not* escaped (`> 0x7F` is false) | [ ] |\n| A11 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ESCAPE_SLASH` off vs on, strings containing `/` | [ ] |\n| A12 | `json_dumps` | short escapes `\\b \\f \\n \\r \\t \\\" \\\\` and `\\u00XX` for the other `< 0x20` control chars | [ ] |\n| A13 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_SORT_KEYS` on — `compare_keys` = `memcmp` over `min(len)` then `len1-len2`; keys sharing prefixes, differing lengths, non-ASCII bytes | [ ] |\n| A14 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_SORT_KEYS` off — insertion order via `ordered_list`; includes overwriting an existing key (position of the *first* insert is retained) | [ ] |\n| A15 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_SORT_KEYS \\| JSON_INDENT(n)` and `JSON_SORT_KEYS \\| JSON_COMPACT` (separate last-element paths: `i < size-1` vs `next != NULL`) | [ ] |\n| A16 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_PRESERVE_ORDER` set and clear — must be byte-identical (no-op flag) | [ ] |\n| A17 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENCODE_ANY` on, root = string / integer / real / true / false / null | [ ] |\n| A18 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_ENCODE_ANY` off, root = array and object (the only accepted roots) | [ ] |\n| A19 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_REAL_PRECISION(p)` for **every** p in 0..31, over randomized finite doubles. p=0 → dtoa mode 0 (shortest round-trip); p≥1 → mode 2; **p in 25..31 makes every real fail** (`dtoa_r` scratch is 25 bytes) | [ ] |\n| A20 | `json_dumps` | reals hitting the exponent switch `decpt <= -4 \\|\\| decpt > 16`; integral doubles forced to `\".0\"`; `-0.0` keeps its sign; huge/tiny magnitudes; subnormals | [ ] |\n| A21 | `json_dumps` | `json_int_t` boundaries `i64::MIN`, `i64::MAX`, 0, ±1, plus randomized | [ ] |\n| A22 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_EMBED` + root array: outer `[`/`]` suppressed; empty embedded array emits **nothing** | [ ] |\n| A23 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_EMBED` + root object: outer `{`/`}` suppressed; empty embedded object emits nothing | [ ] |\n| A24 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_EMBED` + scalar root (bit ignored) and `JSON_EMBED \\| JSON_INDENT(n)` (items still indented one level in) | [ ] |\n| A25 | `json_dumps` | `JSON_EMBED` on a *nested* container — bit is stripped before recursion, so inner brackets are kept | [ ] |\n